<title>USA: Consumers Gas Group Q4 net off.</title>
<headline>Consumers Gas Group Q4 net off.</headline>
<dateline>DEARBORN, Mich. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996    1995</p>
<p>Three Month Ended December 31 (unaudited)</p>
<p> Operating Revenue				   $402    $394</p>
<p> Net Income						15	18</p>
<p>Average Number of Common Shares</p>
<p> Outstanding - G Stock				7.8     7.6</p>
<p> Earnings Per Average Common Share		.44     .55</p>
<p> Dividends Declared per Common Share	   .295     .28</p>
<p>Twelve Months Ended December 31 (unaudited)</p>
<p> Operating Revenue				  1,282   1,195</p>
<p> Net Income						59	62</p>
<p>Average Number of Common Shares</p>
<p> Outstanding - G Stock				7.7     7.5</p>
<p> Earnings per Average Common Share	     1.82    .38*</p>
<p> Dividends Declared per Common Share	   1.15     .56</p>
<p>		 (Millions, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>*Class G Shares were issued on July 21, 1995.  Pro-forma earnings per share, assuming Class G Shares were outstanding for the full year 1995, would be $1.93.</p>
<p>CMS Energy Corp's regulated natural gas utility and storage businesses are represented by CMS Class G stock.</p>
<p>		 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
